---
layout: base.njk
modelLinks:
  - [Docs, 'https://docs.hpvsim.org']
  - [Tutorials, 'https://docs.hpvsim.org/tutorials']
  - [Code, 'https://github.com/starsimhub/hpvsim']
  - [Legacy v2.3, 'https://github.com/starsimhub/hpvsim/releases/tag/v2.3.0']
filters:
  - [all, All]
  - [in-flight, In flight]
  - [peer-reviewed, Peer-reviewed]
  - [publications, Publications]
---
{% from "components.njk" import studyCard, studyHref %}
{% macro secHead(title, desc) %}
<div class="sec-head">
  <h2 class="sec-title">{{ title }}</h2>
  {% if desc %}<p class="sec-desc">{{ desc }}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endmacro %}

<section id="model" class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Agent-based HPV + cervical disease modeling · Built on Starsim</p>
    <h1>HPVsim</h1>
    <p class="lede">
HPVsim is an agent-based model of HPV transmission and progression through cervical disease to cancer. It supports country-specific vital dynamics, structured sexual networks, co-transmitting HPV genotypes, B- and T-cell mediated immunity, and high-resolution disease natural history, plus built-in tools for vaccination, screening, and treatment interventions. It is implemented in pure Python, extensively tested and documented, and runs in seconds to minutes on a laptop.
    </p>
    <p class="versions">
      <strong>v3.0</strong> (released July 2026) is built on the
      <a href="https://starsim.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Starsim</a>
      architecture and is the actively developed line. The pre-Starsim
      <strong>v2.3</strong> release (April 2026) is frozen aside from
      critical bugfixes.
    </p>
    <div class="installs">
      <div class="inst">
        <span class="lbl">Installation</span>
        <code>pip install hpvsim</code>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="links">
      {% for link in modelLinks %}
      <a href="{{ link[1] }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ link[0] }} <i>↗</i></a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="research" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ secHead("Research", "The HPVsim model has been applied to answer questions that broadly fall into four main research themes.") }}

    <div class="themes" role="tablist">
      {% for theme in researchThemeIntros %}
      <button type="button" class="theme" data-f="{{ theme.slug }}">
        <h3>{{ theme.name }}</h3>
        <p>{{ theme.blurb }}</p>
      </button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="chips" role="tablist">
      {% for f in filters %}
      <button class="chip{{ ' on' if loop.first }}" data-f="{{ f[0] }}">{{ f[1] }}</button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      {% for study in collections.studies %}{{ studyCard(study) }}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="countries" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ secHead("Countries", "HPVsim has been calibrated to numerous country contexts, some of which have been part of multi-country studies and others which are in-depth focused analyses looking at informing policy. Not all of these have been published, but the table below has details on how you can get more information about a particular country.") }}
    <div class="countries-wrap">
      <table class="countries">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Country</th>
            <th>Model/analysis details</th>
            <th>Partners</th>
            <th>Publications</th>
            <th>Code/data</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in countries %}
          <tr>
            <td class="country-name">{{ c.name }}</td>
            <td>
              {% for a in c.analyses %}
              <div class="cell-line">
                {% if a.studySlug %}
                {% set s = collections.studies | findStudy(a.studySlug) %}
                <a href="{{ studyHref(s) }}">{{ a.label }}</a>
                {% elif a.label %}
                {{ a.label }}
                {% else %}
                —
                {% endif %}
              </div>
              {% endfor %}
            </td>
            <td>
              {% for a in c.analyses %}<div class="cell-line">{{ a.partners }}</div>{% endfor %}
            </td>
            <td>
              {% for a in c.analyses %}
              <div class="cell-line">
                {% if a.pubHref %}
                <a href="{{ a.pubHref }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ a.pubLabel }} ↗</a>
                {% elif a.pubLabel %}
                {{ a.pubLabel }}
                {% else %}
                —
                {% endif %}
              </div>
              {% endfor %}
            </td>
            <td>
              {% for a in c.analyses %}
              <div class="cell-line">
                {% if a.codeHref %}
                <a href="{{ a.codeHref }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ a.codeLabel }} ↗</a>
                {% else %}
                —
                {% endif %}
              </div>
              {% endfor %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="news" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ secHead("News") }}
    <ul class="news-list">
      {% for item in collections.news %}
      <li class="news-item">
        <span class="news-date">{{ item.data.date | isoDate }}</span>
        <div>
          <h4>{% if item.data.href %}<a href="{{ item.data.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ item.data.title }} <i>↗</i></a>{% else %}{{ item.data.title }}{% endif %}</h4>
          <p>{{ item.data.blurb }}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
